# Build output. `node build.js` writes both dist/ and docs/, and docs/index.html
# is the byte-identical copy GitHub Pages actually serves — so committing dist/
# as well just puts a second half-megabyte of generated file in the repo and
# invites somebody to edit the wrong one.
dist/

# Working documents — these are correspondence, not the project. They contain
